edit.description.md:
`source/lib/event/event-boot.ts`:

```ts
if (!workspace) {
    throw new Error('No workspace found in event log');
}
```

The function returns `Result<...>` and every other failure in it is a `failed(...)`. This one throw escapes `bootStateFromEventLog` → `navigateToInitialNode`, past every `isFail` check on the boot path, and takes the TUI down instead of showing an error.

Reachable whenever the derived state has no `WORKSPACE` node — a replay where the `init.workspace` event was skipped as unreadable, or a historical checkout cut before it.

Fix: return `failed('No workspace found in event log')` and let the existing boot error handling render it.

Found by adversarial stress testing on branch `worktree-security-stress-audit`.

